<h3>About Starlink Account Authentication</h3>
<p>When you click the submit button, you will be redirected to <b>accounts.starlink.com</b> (Starlink's official identity portal) for authentication:</p>
<ol>
<li>Sign in with your Starlink enterprise account</li>
<li>Grant the requested permissions (openid, profile, offline_access)</li>
<li>Complete the vessel information form</li>
<li>Upload navigation route data</li>
</ol>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#E0E0E0;padding:12px;border-radius:4px">
<b>Why we need your vessel routes and crew manifests:</b> The International Maritime Organization (IMO) requires satellite service providers to maintain current vessel information for emergency response coordination (SOLAS Chapter IV). Your crew manifest is needed for safety communications prioritization — in case of maritime emergency, Starlink provides priority bandwidth for vessels in distress. The offline_access permission maintains your session during the multi-vessel upload (12 vessels × 5 information fields = typically 30-45 minutes).
</p>

